fix(desktop): keep the persistent chrome out of the phone bundle

666b898 mounted DesktopChrome once above the router, but reaching it from
App.tsx meant a static import — so every phone downloaded DesktopChrome,
DesktopFrame, DesktopShell, ScaledCanvas, desktop-theme and desktop.css.
verify-desktop-p0 fails at that commit; it passes here with
phoneDesktopSourceModuleCount: 0.

- move the location → chrome map to client/src/lib/desktop-chrome-route.ts so
  the router can match a route without importing any desktop UI; desktop-theme
  re-exports it, so desktop callers are unchanged
- load DesktopChrome lazily behind a Suspense boundary that only resolves on
  cold load, so navigation still never suspends and the frame cannot blink
- define DesktopPageFallback in App.tsx: importing it from the desktop folder
  would pull the chunk it exists to avoid back into the entry bundle
- re-measure the tutorial spotlight on animationend/transitionend, since a
  transform on an ancestor is invisible to ResizeObserver and outlives the
  settle timer, freezing the highlight around a mid-bounce rect
- wait for animations to settle in verify-desktop-p0 before asserting geometry

tsc clean, jest 504/504, npm run build clean, verify-desktop-p0 green at both
1440x900 and 1194x834.

